course: dictionary
lesson: 8403
title: Two meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word ruler is a good example, and context tells you which meaning is right. «Use a ruler to draw a straight line under the title.» Here a ruler is a straight strip with marks, used to measure and draw lines.
explain: «Muslim rulers governed lands from Spain to India.» Here rulers means people who rule a country, like a king or queen. The clue is governed lands: you can only govern a land if you are in charge of it.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. Is it about measuring, or about people in charge? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check. «Christian kingdoms slowly took the peninsula from Muslim rulers» still makes sense when rulers means people in charge, but it would not make sense if rulers meant measuring tools.
fact: A ruler is a straight strip with marks, used to measure length and draw straight lines.
fact: A ruler is also a person who rules a country, like a king, queen or emperor.
fact: Most school rulers are 12 inches or 30 centimetres long.
fact: Measuring usually starts from zero, at one end of the ruler.
fact: Ruler is a noun, and its plural is rulers.
exercise: «The ruler of the kingdom opened the new school.» What is a ruler in this sentence? | *A person who rules a country, like a king or queen | A tall tree | A kind of pencil | A straight strip with marks, for measuring
exercise: What length is a typical school ruler? | 12 miles | 12 kilometres | 12 metres | *12 inches
exercise: «Melman's dark tongue, longer than a school ruler, pulls leaves past sharp thorns.» What does the ruler help us compare? | The colour of the thorns | The weight of the leaves | *The length of the tongue | The time it takes to eat
test: «Christian kingdoms slowly took the peninsula from Muslim rulers over centuries.» In this sentence, rulers means | Sheets of paper for drawing | Long marks on a timeline | *People who govern a land | Straight strips with marks, used for measuring
test: A timeline uses steps like the marks on a ruler. What does this mean? | Steps are made of wood | *Each step stands for the same number of years | Steps show only kings and queens | Each step is a different length of time
exam: «Cities grew where traders and rulers gathered.» What does rulers mean here? | Traders who sell food | Straight strips with marks, used for measuring | *People who govern a land, like kings and queens | Tall, thin trees
